  "interpretation": "<p data-start=\"58\" data-end=\"270\">This test measures <strong data-start=\"77\" data-end=\"121\">mercury levels in a 24-hour urine sample</strong>, used to assess exposure to <strong data-start=\"150\" data-end=\"185\">inorganic and elemental mercury</strong> (e.g. from dental amalgams, mercury thermometers, batteries, or industrial sources).</p>\n<p data-start=\"1182\" data-end=\"1215\">High urinary mercury may suggest:</p>\n<ul data-start=\"1216\" data-end=\"1442\">\n<li data-start=\"1216\" data-end=\"1275\">\n<p data-start=\"1218\" data-end=\"1275\"><strong data-start=\"1218\" data-end=\"1243\">Occupational exposure</strong> (miners, dentists, lab workers)</p>\n</li>\n<li data-start=\"1276\" data-end=\"1346\">\n<p data-start=\"1278\" data-end=\"1346\"><strong data-start=\"1278\" data-end=\"1346\">Use of mercury-containing skin products or traditional medicines</strong></p>\n</li>\n<li data-start=\"1347\" data-end=\"1385\">\n<p data-start=\"1349\" data-end=\"1385\"><strong data-start=\"1349\" data-end=\"1368\">Dental amalgams</strong> (typically mild)</p>\n</li>\n<li data-start=\"1386\" data-end=\"1442\">\n<p data-start=\"1388\" data-end=\"1442\"><strong data-start=\"1388\" data-end=\"1414\">Environmental exposure</strong> (broken thermometers, etc.)</p>\n</li>\n</ul>\n<p>&nbsp;</p>",
